ndu temple...we worship the god named \"shiva ji\"... people have lots of believe in this god...and behind this temple there is a river it's called \"bagmati\" and this is the place to do funeral as well in Hindu style it's called \"dahasanskar\".... \nso you will fell peaceful when you visit this place....", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2BF5466961A7158F3E247555410A8AC6", "name": "Ribita Shahi", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/shahiribita", "username": "shahiribita", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/79/default-avatar-2020-21.jpg", "contribution_count": 17, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 189100, "location_name": "Portugal", "location_name_detailed": "Portugal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-15", "published_at_date": "2017-09-16"}, {"review_id": 524634655, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r524634655-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Place to see !!", "text": "For Hindus this Temple is the most important place to visit, like Mecca for Muslims.\nYou can see cremation also, I came with an experienced guide, much better", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B1C11D74D567E655AF9CB22C3B5600F5", "name": "Enzo M", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/claudepour", "username": "claudepour", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/06/default-avatar-2020-18.jpg", "contribution_count": 598, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187147, "location_name": "Paris", "location_name_detailed": "Paris, France"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/aa/b6/86/img-20170911-155348-largejpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/aa/b6/87/img-20170911-160409-largejpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/aa/b6/89/img-20170911-160413-largejpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-09-15", "published_at_date": "2017-09-16"}, {"review_id": 523993813, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523993813-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Varanasi in Nepal", "text": "Despite the main temple being only open to Hindus, the whole area is a place of wonder. From the cremations in the river side to the monkeys in the hill, Pashupatinath is another one of the \"must see\" of Kathmandu.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "50826DD1627282EE0A6E3514C0BF341E", "name": "Tomàs N", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/tom_sn306", "username": "tom_sn306", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/6d/default-avatar-2020-19.jpg", "contribution_count": 6, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-13", "published_at_date": "2017-09-14"}, {"review_id": 523912274, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523912274-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Go in the evening!", "text": "We pay the crazy 1000 rupees fee. The place is pretty amazing. We get there by 6 and we can experience one cremation and  the amazing dancing and music show across the river. This made all worth it. It happens every day from 7pm to 8pm aprox. Every body crazy dancing and screaming with priests holding big fire candels. Very cool. Regarding the cremation, everybody knows is a public place and that they will be people taking pictures and all. The family pay a great deal of money to do this ritual and they are perfectly aware of tourists and all. If they want a private place there is one. But here is open for public and every body knows it. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9987F9EEBC4AE196D7FE9BEFCE98523B", "name": "SantiagoBecker", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/SantiagoBecker", "username": "SantiagoBecker", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/b8/default-avatar-2020-26.jpg", "contribution_count": 21, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-13", "published_at_date": "2017-09-13"}, {"review_id": 523907572, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523907572-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Wonderful temple with a very old history.....", "text": "Very very old Lord shiva temple, it is really very beautiful and spiritual place, for Hindus it is one of the most important place to visit, it is said that lord shiva is present in active form in this temple, this temple has a very beautiful Bharavnath, Ganpati and Hanuman Idols, even there are so many small shiv lungs all around the main temple. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "75BB2626B7B275C21ACC2641F23CA423", "name": "Gaurav S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/gauravs129", "username": "gauravs129", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/e3/default-avatar-2020-59.jpg", "contribution_count": 287, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 297612, "location_name": "Surat", "location_name_detailed": "Surat, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/a4/2b/3b/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/a4/2b/3c/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/a4/2b/3d/photo2jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/a4/2b/3f/photo3jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/a4/2b/40/photo4jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/a4/2b/41/photo5jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-09-13", "published_at_date": "2017-09-13"}, {"review_id": 523803751, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523803751-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Sacred", "text": "I had mixed feelings about visiting this place. It was such an educational experience to learn about and see first-hand Hindu death rituals. Being from the US, where grief and the whole business of death are intensely private, it felt intrusive to witness what we saw here. I still feel it was one of the most important parts of our visit and I'm thankful for the experience.\n\nWe visited during Tihar in 2014 and again in 2016. Tihar was indescribable. The day we visited Pashupatinath was the day they worshipped dogs. There were dogs lounging on the stairs with tika on their foreheads and garlands of marigolds around their necks.\n\nWe saw people being cremated on the banks of the Bagmati, and learned about the two sides of the bridge. Life and death are linked here, and it was beautiful to see another culture's handling of this inevitable part of life.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2016-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C17505C2664AB8CC95717CF138D32935", "name": "JessB24", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/JessB24", "username": "JessB24", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/b6/e9/f9/jessb24.jpg", "contribution_count": 78, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 43323, "location_name": "Minneapolis", "location_name_detailed": "Minneapolis, Minnesota"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-12", "published_at_date": "2017-09-13"}, {"review_id": 523403180, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523403180-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Cremation of my best friends father 91@ RIP KAKA", "text": "Sad SAD day for my friend, as her father passed away due to illness so he was taken to the crematorium, a newly built but in dire straits as all things are in Nepal. Not very clean, out of 2 one not working and one has to wait for more than an hour to get a turn. Parking area poorly maintained and very very sad to see such conditions of the new crematorium dunno where all the FUNDS go?", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AC0CA5D71E81F0AD3E3EE629169C5519", "name": "Sherpa Lama Dawa", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/daffodilktm", "username": "daffodilktm", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/27/a1/91/e9/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 479, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/9f/ce/5b/photo0jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-09-11", "published_at_date": "2017-09-12"}, {"review_id": 523342017, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523342017-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "So disappointed to see temple condition :(", "text": "Pashupatinath temple is one of holy places for Hindu and it's one of 12 Jyolingas. It was sad to see how poorly temple was maintained.\n\nNo signs of directions within temple. Temple premise is not at all clean and it was stinking. It was devastating to see such a holy place in this condition. Hope Nepal tourism will do well maintenance for their leading attractions.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 2, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "768A46A8A19D28757E75E2AE32137593", "name": "Himcream", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Himcream2015", "username": "Himcream2015", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/3c/9c/52/himcream2015.jpg", "contribution_count": 287, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294265, "location_name": "Singapore", "location_name_detailed": "Singapore, Singapore"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-09-11", "published_at_date": "2017-09-11"}, {"review_id": 523285573, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r523285573-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Amazing experience that gave me an insight into Hinduism ", "text": "This has been the highlight of my visit so far simply because I got to learn so much about Hinduism and also the burial practices. I would strongly recommend going with a guide to provide you with some of the context and also to explain in particular what you can see unfold before your eyes. Whilst the temple when approached seems a bit chaotic and dirty and in some areas affected by the great earthquake of 2015, it is worth holding judgement until you get to the banks of the river to see the throngs of people either sitting down with the Brahims to honour the parents who has passed in yesteryear or those people who were there to bide farewell to loved ones who had recently passed away. The burial rituals were very visual and telling from the washing of the feet of dead with the holy river waters, to the preparation of the funeral pyres on which the dead where then cremated on the banks of the river. This was a very visually rich scene and at times quite sad as you saw family members breakdown as the weight of the loss of their lost one became too much\n\nI was thankful to have the guide unpick all that was going on and also position this with the context of the Hindu religion\n\nDo not miss this!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "F62953A59DC8008A153701001E6DC057", "name": "EkeneE", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/EkeneE", "username": "EkeneE", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f0/d5/default-avatar-2020-17.jpg", "contribution_count": 171, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186338, "location_name": "London", "location_name_detailed": "London, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/